            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CLV14"} CLV 14
            %a{:href => "#YangLiu18"} Yang-Liu 18
            …
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#Classification Classification
          %h4#spatial_symmetries Spatial symmetries
          %p
            Symmetry protected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystal"} crystalline
            phases where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            may approximately be regarded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free
            (but subject to the the atomic lattice Coulomb
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+field"} background field
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Dirac+field#FreeDiracFieldInCoulombBackground"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+equivariant+K-theory"} twisted equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
          %p
            Beware that this case has mostly been discussed for CPT-symmetries such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-reversal+symmetry"} time-reversal symmetry
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulator"} topological insulator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystallographic+group"} crystallographic symmetries
            (see at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+crystalline+insulator"} topological crystalline insulator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+symmetry"} internal
            (“on site”) symmetries (but see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Wen12"} Wen 12
          %h4#ClassificationInternalSymmetries Internal symmetries
          %p
            In contrast, a widely cited claim
            %a{:href => "#CGLW11"} CGLW 11
            asserts (motivation is offered in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CLW11"} CLW 11, Sec. V
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %em bosonic
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+symmetry"} internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+group"} symmetry group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi int
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{int}
            are given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
